## 2. Ship 2 — launch --exec

Leftover: --exec runs sh -c "test -e PATH; exit 0" and prints
ooda launch: ok. fixtures/pm_launch_exec/runme.oo never runs.
main of that pin prints LAUNCH_EXEC_OK.

Would still pass if the bug remained:
  ./bin/ooda launch --exec runme ; test $? -eq 0
  (test -e succeeds because the CAS leaf exists)

How SK1 fails that leftover: ingest, then require LAUNCH_EXEC_OK
only on --exec. test -e cannot print LAUNCH_EXEC_OK.

CRIT-S2 — new shell each time. Prior ingest. OODA_FS_WRITEDIR=$PWD.

    export OODA_FS_WRITEDIR="$(pwd)"
    ./bin/ooda ingest --from fixtures/pm_launch_exec

  2026-08-17T19:20:28-04:00  exit 0
    ooda ingest: installed runme cas=95a48b4d1875327343bbf8e29d6457c5a0eadc2c29f969917513226b76483ecd

    ./bin/ooda launch runme

  Run 1 and run 2, both exit 0:
    ooda launch: ok /home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-cli-three/.ooda_modules/cas/95a48b4d1875327343bbf8e29d6457c5a0eadc2c29f969917513226b76483ecd/runme.oo
    LAUNCH_EXEC_OK absent (0 hits).

    timeout 60 ./bin/ooda launch --exec runme

  Run 1 2026-08-17T19:20:39-04:00  exit 0
    LAUNCH_EXEC_OK
    OK
  Run 2 2026-08-17T19:20:49-04:00  exit 0
    LAUNCH_EXEC_OK
    OK

The payload printed LAUNCH_EXEC_OK. The second OK is oodac run, not
the old launch stub. Path-only never ran main. Revert to test -e
exits 0 and never prints LAUNCH_EXEC_OK. That fails this CRIT.

Supporting, not sufficient: `strings ./bin/ooda | grep -F 'test -e '`
is empty. Behavior above is the proof.

## 3. Ship 3 — bench

